WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.238
Step 3 collects Azure from
the day-one fixtures.

2
00:00:03.238 --> 00:00:06.241
Five notices, all open,
two needing action,

3
00:00:06.241 --> 00:00:11.012
one of each kind but change, and
every one valid against the schema.

4
00:00:11.012 --> 00:00:13.812
Notice: five notices from six rows.

5
00:00:13.812 --> 00:00:17.562
The incident's rows from two
subscriptions became one notice.

6
00:00:17.562 --> 00:00:20.062
Step 4 reads the records as a table.

7
00:00:20.062 --> 00:00:23.689
The retirement of basic
public IP addresses

8
00:00:23.689 --> 00:00:26.924
is action required by September 30, 2027.

9
00:00:26.924 --> 00:00:30.537
The security advisory is
action required with no date.

10
00:00:30.537 --> 00:00:34.812
The incident, the advisory and the
planned maintenance need no action,

11
00:00:34.812 --> 00:00:36.940
and they'll go to the weekly digest.
